# Task as a Mental Model

Task is a conceptual tool or principle that helps understand and navigate complex situations. It provides a mental shortcut or framework for making sense of patterns and relationships in the world.

## Definition

Task functions as a universal mental model applicable across all domains. It serves as a meta-framework for framing work, projects, and commitments, offering a way to recognize patterns and relationships within complex situations.

## Cross-Source Perspectives

This mental model is referenced in [[Getting Things Done - David Allen]] by David Allen, where it functions as a universal shortcut for navigating complexity through structured approach to work and commitments.

